@prefix : <#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix folio: <https://pkg.semvia.io/semvia/folio/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rml: <http://w3id.org/rml/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix svrl: <https://pkg.semvia.io/semvia/rml/lookup#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
:BattingStints rml:logicalSource <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-logicalsource> ;
	rml:predicateObjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-atbats> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-doubles> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-games> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-hits> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-homeruns> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-player> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-runsbattedin> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-stintordinal> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-stolenbases> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-strikeouts> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-teamseason> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-triples> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-walks> ;
	rml:subjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/BattingStints-subjectmap> ;
	a rml:TriplesMap ;
	rdfs:comment "One bball:Stint per row of public.batting — 128,598 rows, injective on the\nfour-column subject template.\nstint is spliced raw into the subject and cast to ordinal for querying; the\ntemplate needs the text and a comparison needs the integer, and one column cannot\nbe both. c_2b and c_3b are the register's spelling of doubles and triples,\nprefixed because a CSV header cannot start an identifier with a digit — the\nconceptual names drop the survivor prefix along with the abbreviation." ;
	rdfs:label "BattingStints" .
:FieldingStints rml:logicalSource <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-logicalsource> ;
	rml:predicateObjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-assists> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-errors> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-player> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-putouts> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-teamseason> ;
	rml:subjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/FieldingStints-subjectmap> ;
	a rml:TriplesMap ;
	rdfs:comment "One bball:Stint per row of public.fielding — but 174,332 rows over 127,079\ndistinct stints, because the register records a separate row per position\nplayed. The subject template does not splice pos, so a stint spent at two\npositions carries two putout counts, two assist counts and two error counts on\none resource.\nThat is the honest projection of a source whose grain is finer than the entity's,\nand the bball:Stint shape declines to cap those paths at 1 for exactly that\nreason: a cap would report the register as invalid when what is actually true is\nthat the model is one level coarser than the table. A query that wants per-\nposition putouts, assists or errors needs a resource per position, which this\npackage does not mint — bball:PositionAppearance carries games at a position\nand nothing else; a query that wants a stint's fielding total needs SUM, not a\nlookup.\nThis map does not emit bball:position. The appearances pivot below does,\non its own subject, at the grain the position code actually keys — see the note\nthere." ;
	rdfs:label "FieldingStints" .
:PitchingStints rml:logicalSource <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-logicalsource> ;
	rml:predicateObjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-earnedrunaverage> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-losses> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-player> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-saves> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-teamseason> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-wins> ;
	rml:subjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PitchingStints-subjectmap> ;
	a rml:TriplesMap ;
	rdfs:comment "One bball:Stint per row of public.pitching — 57,630 rows, minting the same\nsubject as the batting stint it always shares a key with.\nFour predicates only, all of them unambiguous on a stint: no batting line carries\nwins, losses, saves or an earned run average. Hits allowed, innings pitched and\nthe rest of the pitching line need predicates of their own before they can be\nmapped, and they do not have them yet." ;
	rdfs:label "PitchingStints" .
:PositionAppearances rml:logicalSource <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-logicalsource> ;
	rml:predicateObjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-gamesatposition> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-player> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-position> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-stint> , <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-teamseason> ;
	rml:subjectMap <stints/.well-known/genid/markdown/PositionAppearances-subjectmap> ;
	a rml:TriplesMap ;
	rdfs:comment "The unflatten. public.appearances is one row per player-season-team with\nthirteen position columns side by side — g_p, g_c, g_1b, g_2b,\ng_3b, g_ss, g_lf, g_cf, g_rf, g_of, g_dh, g_ph, g_pr — a\nspreadsheet shape, not a relational one. RDF has no column position, so the\npredicate would have to be bball:gamesAtShortstop, bball:gamesAtCatcher and\neleven more: thirteen predicates encoding one dimension, and a query asking \"what\nposition did they play\" unable to be written without naming all thirteen.\nThe rml:SQL2008Query source below turns the columns into rows — thirteen\nUNION ALL branches, one per position, each lifting the position code into a\npos value and the count into gamesatposition. One predicate pair comes out:\nbball:position and bball:gamesAtPosition, paired one-to-one per row — and one\nsubject per row to keep them paired." ;
	rdfs:label "PositionAppearances" .
